{
  "requirement": "Distinguishes a domain operation failure, a missing agent, an agent failure, and an error encoding or decoding the output.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum ValidationError<E> {\n    Graph(E),\n    NoAgentConfigured,\n    Agent(String),\n    Output(serde_json::Error),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<E: Debug> Debug for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Display> Display for ValidationError<E>;\nimpl<E: Error + 'static> Error for ValidationError<E>;\n```",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the four variants are well tested. The `Display` and `Error` trait implementations have no test marked for this requirement.\n\n**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.validators.ValidationError`:**\n1. The enum distinguishes `Graph(E)`, `NoAgentConfigured`, `Agent(String)` and `Output(serde_json::Error)`.\n2. It implements `Debug`, `Display` and `Error` with the stated bounds.\n\n**Covered:**\n- **`Graph` and `Output`:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[refresh_propagates_load_decode_check_execution_and_save_errors]` is marked `{test}`. It matches `ValidationError::Output(_)` for the decode and stale-decode stages. For the load, read, edges, execute and store stages it matches `ValidationError::Graph(actual)` and asserts `actual` equals the stage name. The `Output` and `Graph` variants stay distinct. Its `{other:?}` panic message also uses the `Debug` impl.\n- **`NoAgentConfigured`:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` is marked `{test}`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)` when no agent is set, and that nothing is stored.\n- **`Agent`:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` is marked `{test}`. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Agent(_))` from both `ctx.ask` and `verify`, and that no record is stored.\n- **Exports:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` is marked `{test}` and checks the exported item inventory.\n\n**Gap (marking):**\n- None of the four marked tests exercises the `Display` or `Error` implementations. They only compile against the type, and `Debug` is used only in a panic message.\n- A test that does exercise them exists, but it is not marked for this requirement. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload]` checks `to_string()` on `Agent`, `source().is_none()`, and `source()` on `Graph`. It carries only `{test}` for `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.execute`.\n- The requirement lists `Display` and `Error` as part of its text. A relevant test without a `{test}` reference to the subject is a marking gap.\n- No test is marked for the `source()` mapping of the `Output` and `NoAgentConfigured` variants. The requirement does not spell that mapping out, so I did not count it as a separate gap.\n\n**Fix:** add `{test}` for `requirements.sdk.graph.validators.ValidationError` to `agent_errors_expose_the_agreed_string_payload`.",
